Test Code
11 April 2026
EPE 05 Test C1
Engineering Family
FSEPE
Substrate:
Cushioned Vinyl (standard)

Adhesive:
Hot-melt adhesive

Upper layer:
Kitchen foil

Method Summary:
An attempt was made to attach kitchen foil to standard floor vinyl using the hot-melt adhesive cut to the size of the A5 size floor vinyl piece using an iron to heat the surface.

Observed Behaviours:
-The enormous heat and pressure caused the cushioned vinyl to lose its foam qualities. It basically became a standard, if thick, vinyl layer.
- The adhesive stuck to neither the foil NOR the flattened cushioned vinyl layer.

Outcome State
Terminal Fail

Lineage Notes
This was the first FSEP test, with a date and time (it was performed a day before this report was written). 

 Cross References
It was the first test in this family of tests and so it has no comparison to other tests.

Doctrinal Implications
This test showed that
[1] heat and pressure reduce considerably the foam-like characteristic of floor vinyl when applied directly with an iron directly to the cushioned vinyl.
[2] hot-melt adhesive will not stick to kitchen foil.
[3] hot-melt adhesive will be less likely to stick to cushioned vinyl.


